  },
  {
   "id": "q8q4hik6xu2tx0t0c9",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 72,
   "y": 5204,
   "width": 1446,
   "height": 113.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#5f3a00",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 770212,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 690001,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why 404 and not 403: a 403 confirms the resource exists, which leaks the id space of other tenants. Returning 404 makes \u201cbelongs to someone else\u201d and \u201cdoes not exist\u201d indistinguishable.\n\nDefence in depth \u2014 four independent layers, any one of which would stop the leak:\n1. orgId is taken only from the verified JWT. A client-supplied organizationId in body or query is ignored everywhere, and its presence is logged as suspicious.\n2. Service functions cannot be called without an orgId \u2014 it is a required positional parameter, so omitting it is a TypeScript compile error, not a runtime bug.\n3. Integration tests assert isolation per resource type; CI fails if any endpoint returns another org's row.\n4. Postgres row-level security policies are defined as a backstop, so even a hand-written query outside the service layer cannot cross tenants.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "dlebz0whz3wiuojf5w",
   "originalText": "Why 404 and not 403: a 403 confirms the resource exists, which leaks the id space of other tenants. Returning 404 makes \u201cbelongs to someone else\u201d and \u201cdoes not exist\u201d indistinguishable.\n\nDefence in depth \u2014 four independent layers, any one of which would stop the leak:\n1. orgId is taken only from the verified JWT. A client-supplied organizationId in body or query is ignored everywhere, and its presence is logged as suspicious.\n2. Service functions cannot be called without an orgId \u2014 it is a required positional parameter, so omitting it is a TypeScript compile error, not a runtime bug.\n3. Integration tests assert isolation per resource type; CI fails if any endpoint returns another org's row.\n4. Postgres row-level security policies are defined as a backstop, so even a hand-written query outside the service layer cannot cross tenants.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "baseline": 13
  },
